            <ArticleTitle>Neurosurgical management of neuropathic pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>76-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Neuropathic pain is a very difficult problem with which the neurosurgeon frequently must deal. The neurosurgical methods to be considered are: (1) modulative, by using neurostimulation or implanted drug delivery systems, and (2) ablative, by making selective therapeutic lesions in well-defined and identified targets proven to sustain pain mechanisms (especially DREZotomy).</AbstractText>
